1
00:00:10,900 --> 00:00:17,580
A Night in the Mountains Although it was autumn, the snow was already

2
00:00:17,580 --> 00:00:19,320
beginning to fall in Tibet.

3
00:00:19,980 --> 00:00:25,040
Our legs were so heavy and cold that they felt like blocks of ice.

4
00:00:25,880 --> 00:00:28,660
Have you ever seen snowmen ride bicycles?

5
00:00:28,660 --> 00:00:30,960
That’s what we looked like!

6
00:00:31,620 --> 00:00:36,740
Along the way children dressed in long wool coats stopped to look at us.

7
00:00:37,680 --> 00:00:43,360
In the late afternoon we found it was so cold that our water bottles froze.

8
00:00:44,140 --> 00:00:49,280
However, the lakes shone like glass in the setting sun and looked wonderful.

9
00:00:50,460 --> 00:00:52,820
Wang Wei rode in front of me as usual.

10
00:00:53,260 --> 00:00:57,560
She is very reliable and I knew I didn’t need to encourage her.

11
00:00:58,060 --> 00:01:02,240
To climb the mountains was hard work but as we looked around us,

12
00:01:02,240 --> 00:01:04,440
we were surprised by the view.

13
00:01:04,820 --> 00:01:07,740
We seemed to be able to see for miles.

14
00:01:08,280 --> 00:01:13,840
At one point we were so high that we found ourselves cycling through clouds.

15
00:01:14,540 --> 00:01:17,000
Then we began going down the hills.

16
00:01:17,580 --> 00:01:22,400
It was great fun especially as it gradually became much warmer.

17
00:01:23,400 --> 00:01:29,580
In the valleys colorful butterflies flew around us and we saw many yaks

18
00:01:29,580 --> 00:01:31,660
and sheep eating green grass.

19
00:01:32,360 --> 00:01:35,400
At this point we had to change our caps,

20
00:01:35,700 --> 00:01:39,520
coats, gloves and trousers for T-shirts and shorts.

21
00:01:44,160 --> 00:01:46,840
We put up our tent and then we eat.

22
00:01:46,840 --> 00:01:52,440
After supper Wang Wei put her head down on her pillow and went to sleep

23
00:01:52,440 --> 00:01:54,020
but I stayed awake.

24
00:01:54,680 --> 00:01:59,440
At midnight the sky became clearer and the stars grew brighter.

25
00:01:59,960 --> 00:02:01,840
It was so quiet.

26
00:02:02,200 --> 00:02:07,300
There was almost no wind - only the flames of our fire for company.

27
00:02:21,920 --> 00:02:23,740
We can hardly wait to see them!
